They all use basically the same procedure.  If it complains about
not being able to find source files, try opening the patch file in
a text editor and changing the file paths to use the same directory
name as your toplevel nethack directory.

e.g. if your nethack directory is just "nethack", change this:
diff -bNurd nethack-3.4.3/dat/opthelp nh343dump/dat/opthelp
--- nethack-3.4.3/dat/opthelp	2003-12-08 01:39:13.000000000 +0200
+++ nh343dump/dat/opthelp	2009-01-11 11:36:04.000000000 +0200

...to this:

diff -bNurd nethack/dat/opthelp nh343dump/dat/opthelp
--- nethack/dat/opthelp	2003-12-08 01:39:13.000000000 +0200
+++ nh343dump/dat/opthelp	2009-01-11 11:36:04.000000000 +0200

wherever similar lines appear.  I think there's also a command line
option that can make that unnecessary, but this approach is what
I use.


